      "question_id": "Q1",
      "question": "What system or method does the organizer use to check room availability and submit the reservation — for example, a calendar application, a dedicated room booking platform, or a manual process?",
      "answer": "The organizer relies on two interconnected tools: a scheduling tool that tracks appointments and a dedicated space-booking platform. Together they allow the organizer to see which rooms are free at a given time and to formally claim a room. Both tools work in tandem to support the end-to-end process."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q2",
      "question": "Is any approval required before a room reservation is confirmed, and if so, who grants that approval and under what conditions?",
      "answer": "An approval step is not specified in the process. The organizer appears to confirm the booking directly without requiring sign-off from a manager or facilities administrator. No conditional approval criteria are described."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q3",
      "question": "What happens when the requested room is unavailable at the desired time — does the organizer manually search for alternatives, or does the system suggest other options?",
      "answer": "When no suitable space is free, the process treats this as an exception that must be handled, but the specific mechanism — whether the organizer hunts manually or the platform proposes alternatives — is not defined. It is simply flagged as a known exception case."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q4",
      "question": "How is the confirmed room information shared with participants — through an automatic calendar invitation, a separate email or message, or some other method?",
      "answer": "After securing the room, the organizer creates or updates a calendar invite and then separately sends a notification to attendees with the room details. Both a scheduling invite and a direct communication via a messaging or email tool are used."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q5",
      "question": "What is the process when an organizer needs to cancel or reschedule a confirmed room reservation — what steps are taken and who is notified?",
      "answer": "Cancellation and rescheduling are not detailed in the described process. A reservation conflict is acknowledged as a possible exception, but the exact corrective steps and who receives notice in that situation are not specified."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q6",
      "question": "What room attributes does the organizer specify or filter by when searching for availability, such as seating capacity, required equipment, or physical location?",
      "answer": "The organizer considers how many people will attend, whether any special technology or equipment is needed, and where the room should be located. These three criteria — headcount, gear requirements, and preferred location — guide the selection of an appropriate space."
    }
  ]
}
